// Enums.schema — the enum family: all three declaration forms (SPEC §4.2).
// Canonical form only — 0 = None implicit, variants dense from 1, never sparse,
// never explicit values. The distinction between the forms lives at the TYPE:
//
//   enum        with-None: None = 0 rides the wire, range [0, Max]
//   enum_index  index of valid values: wire = value - 1, range [0, Max - 1];
//               storage keeps 0 as an unset sentinel, never wire-legal
//   enum_flags  one bit per variant from bit 0, up to 64; storage uint64 in
//               every target; wire = variant-count raw bits; no implicit None
//               (the empty mask is 0 and needs no name)
//
// Aspect-oriented layout (SPEC §2): one aspect per file.
//
// NOTE (Glenn, 2026-08-05): some of these are flatbuffers residue — hand-declared
// only because flatbuffers gave no better tool. The *Type sets are really DERIVED
// (each config/asset definition defines one), and when the Config/Assets layer
// lands they are GENERATED — the same set-extraction move as MessageType and
// ObjectType. Hand-declared enums remain for genuinely hand-owned sets (Team).

package example

// nullable on the wire — a team field can be "no team"
enum Team { Red Blue }

// index kinds — the create-path pattern: None never rides the wire
enum_index CraftKind   { Light Medium Heavy }
enum_index ShipType    { Fighter Corvette Bomber Destroyer Carrier }
enum_index MissileType { Heatseeker Torpedo Nuke }
enum_index PropType    { Asteroid Chunk Fragment Sphere BlackHole DysonPanel }

// demo-local, used by the switch idiom in Types.schema
enum RecordKind { Craft Debris }

// flags — named bits over a uint64, consumed as masks
enum_flags ShipFlags { FiringLaser Boosting Braking Aiming }
